omics bullies Peter  Parker but ironically admire spider-man  as a hero what he looks out for the  neighborhood has a dope suit in my  really respective sup dickwad and of  course how can we forget Peters best  friend Ned awesome which leads our first  surprising reveal the return of Nick  Fury considering Fury died after the  events of infinity war it seems like the  character will be brought back to life  and judging by his first words so nice  to finally meet you  spider-man it seems as though they do  not encounter each other in endgame and  is this figure next to fury Maria Hill  also brought back from the dead or  someone else entirely a character  obviously missing from the trailer is  none other than Tony Stark who is  heavily featured with spider-man in both  his first appearance in Civil War and  homecoming and this line from Hogan all  alone sounds quite ominous but this be  hinting at the death of Tony Stark and  Avengers and game or maybe it's just  Marvel trying to throw us off the plot  whatever happens the future doesn't look  so promising for Iron Man also featured  in the trailer are the many suits Peter  wears during his trip in Europe in the  beginning Peter where's the classic red  and blue suit that we saw in homecoming  of course things don't go according to  plan as Nick Fury makes an appearance to  set Peter on a mission we see two main  suits featured in the trailer one suit  that closely resembles the classic suit  but with a darker palette and wings the  same wings we only briefly saw in  homecoming are now featured more  prominently seemingly allowing Peter to  effortlessly glide through the sky we  also get a better look at the noir suit  from the spider-man noir series set in  1933 also featured recently in  spider-man into the spider-verse  voiced by Nicolas Cage judging by the  nighttime setting maybe this is the suit  of choice when the job requires stealth  over well aesthetics it was long rumored  that a group of villains known as